  (h)       Multi-decoder roundtrip 4/4                  N/A (gate reverted)

DISCRIMINATOR WORKS PERFECTLY
==============================

  Mode comparison         Cells       byte-identical
  ------------------     ------      ---------------
  Total                  72          63 (87.5%)
  TARGET (1418519)        9           0 ← all 9 changed (gate fires)
  PROTECT (1025469)      15          15 (100%) ← gate correctly rejects
  SPOT (4 photos)        48          48 (100%) ← gate correctly rejects

Hash-locks: 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL (gate cannot fire on synthetic 32×32
fixtures — mask plane not computed, gate degrades to off).

PER-CELL DETAIL on 1418519 (the only image where gate fires)
=============================================================

  cell                 Δbytes      Δssim2      verdict
  ------------------   ---------   ---------   ------------------
  1418519 e7 d=4       -3.43%      +0.0976     win
  1418519 e8 d=4       -2.82%      +0.5172     strong win
  1418519 e9 d=4       -3.08%      +0.5460     strong win
  1418519 e7 d=5       -0.29%      +0.3764     win
  1418519 e8 d=5       +0.68%      +1.1305     strong win
  1418519 e9 d=5       +1.07%      +1.1305     strong win
  1418519 e7 d=6       +4.27%      +0.0696     bytes regress, no SSIM2
  1418519 e8 d=6       +4.62%      +0.2787     bytes regress, weak SSIM2
  1418519 e9 d=6       +4.31%      +0.2787     bytes regress, weak SSIM2

d=4 cluster: -2.8 to -3.4% bytes AND +0.10 to +0.55 SSIM2 — universal win.
d=5 cluster: at parity bytes AND +0.38 to +1.13 SSIM2 — strong win at e8+.
d=6 cluster: +4.3 to +4.6% bytes for only +0.07 to +0.28 SSIM2 — REGRESSION.

The d=6 cells drag the d=5/6 mean from a clear win (d=5 mean = +0.871) down
to +0.544, FAILING the +1.0 hard gate that the task spec required (50%
closure of the W44-147-measured -2.17/-2.57 SSIM2 deficit).

WHY THE D=6 CELLS LOSE BYTES
==============================

At d=6 the libjxl-faithful entropy_mul table's dct32x32=1.48 was already
selecting DCT32X32 aggressively for 1418519's flat regions (mask=92). The
W44-151 lift (1.34) shifts MORE blocks to DCT32X32, but at d=6 the quantizer
is so coarse that those new DCT32X32 picks produce MORE non-zero
coefficients (due to LF-band quantization spread) than the DCT16X16 splits
they replace. The +4.3-4.6% bytes is the cost of those extra non-zero LF
coefficients. The marginal SSIM2 recovery (+0.07 to +0.28) is small because
DCT32X32's spatial averaging at d=6 already produces visible blocking on
1418519's mid-frequency texture; pushing more blocks into that mode doesn't
help quality.

HONEST-STOP DISPOSITION
========================

Per W44-151 task spec, gate REVERTED. The change to:

  jxl-encoder/src/vardct/encoder.rs:
    - `W44_151_HIGH_MASK_P25_MIN = 85.0` constant: KEPT (documentation +
      reuse — see W44-152+ candidates below)
    - `compute_profile_for_search` signature extension (added
      `mask1x1_p25: Option<f32>` parameter): KEPT (passes p25 through
      so future chunks don't need plumbing rewire)
    - W44-151 OR-branch in both inline dispatch (encode_inner) and helper
      (compute_profile_for_search): REVERTED to a no-op (env hook removed,
      branch returns false unconditionally) — the constant + helper +
      threading remain so a follow-on chunk can re-enable with a
      tighter gate.
    - `percentile_mask1x1` helper: KEPT non-dead (consumed by
      `mask1x1_p25` plumbing even though gate is no-op).
  jxl-encoder/src/vardct/bitstream.rs:
    - `mask1x1_p25_for_search` compute: KEPT (negligible cost, threaded
      through helper).
  jxl-encoder/examples/w44_151_w44_29_widen_ab.rs: KEPT as measurement
    reproducer. Env hook `JXL_W44_151_DISABLE=1` no longer wired since
    both modes are byte-identical post-revert.
  jxl-encoder/examples/w44_151_decoder_check.rs: KEPT — produces files
    via the default path (now byte-identical to the legacy path), so
    PASS is trivial.
  docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md Section B: W44-151 row added with HONEST-STOP
